    category: "Poetry",
    emoji: "🐌",
    excerpt: "A slow little snail finds a clever way to finally see the wide world beyond his garden wall.",
    created_at: "2026-04-03T18:00:00Z",
    body: "<p style='color:#6a4b8f;font-style:italic;margin-bottom:18px'>By Khyati Srivastava</p><p>A snail named Sid was much too slow,<br>he longed to see the world below,<br>but inch by inch the days would crawl,<br>he never made it past the wall.</p><p>One day he found a fallen note,<br>a stamp, an address someone wrote,<br>so Sid climbed up with all his might,<br>and stuck himself on tight and right.</p><p>The postman came, he could not tell,<br>and mailed the snail and shiny shell,<br>through busy towns and rolling hills,<br>past rivers, fields, and windowsills.</p><p>At last the letter found its end,<br>a garden owned by Sid's old friend,<br>who opened up the envelope,<br>and gasped with joy and wild hope.</p><p>So Sid had traveled near and far,<br>by mail he sailed beneath the stars,<br>and learned that even being slow,<br>can take you anywhere you go.</p>",
