    emoji: "🌙",
    excerpt: "Tired of glowing all night, the weary moon asks the stars for one evening off, with a surprising result.",
    created_at: "2026-04-03T00:00:00Z",
    body: "<p style='color:#6a4b8f;font-style:italic;margin-bottom:18px'>By Khyati Srivastava</p><p>The moon was tired, so tired of light,<br>of glowing soft through every night,<br>I want a nap, she yawned up high,<br>just one small rest across the sky.</p><p>The stars all blinked, they understood,<br>and told her resting would be good,<br>we will take turns and shine instead,<br>now go and rest your silver head.</p><p>So down she dipped behind a cloud,<br>the stars shone bright, the stars shone proud,<br>they twinkled hard the whole night through,<br>and did their very best to do.</p><p>But oh, the world looked up and sighed,<br>without the moon the dark felt wide,<br>the children missed her gentle beam,<br>that watched them softly in their dream.</p><p>At dawn the moon woke, fresh and bright,<br>and promised she would shine each night,<br>for rest is good, she came to learn,<br>but so is taking up your turn.</p>",
